From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 17:13:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(notifications): destroy a notification timer whose
 notification is gone

Backport of pctrade/end4-pC 584cd9e
https://github.com/pctrade/end4-pC/commit/584cd9e
Problem: NotifTimer fires after its notification was dismissed or discarded; findIndex returns -1 and notifObject.isTransient throws a TypeError, which also skips destroy().
Port: clean (offset)
Drop when: the pinned NotifTimer.onTriggered returns when its notification is no longer in the list.
---
 dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Notifications.qml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Notifications.qml b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Notifications.qml
index 7f09ad51..98aec0f0 100644
--- a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Notifications.qml
+++ b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Notifications.qml
@@ -66,6 +66,11 @@ Singleton {
         running: true
         onTriggered: () => {
             const index = root.list.findIndex((notif) => notif.notificationId === notificationId);
+            // Already dismissed or discarded while the timer was running
+            if (index === -1) {
+                destroy();
+                return;
+            }
             const notifObject = root.list[index];
             print("[Notifications] Notification timer triggered for ID: " + notificationId + ", transient: " + notifObject?.isTransient);
             if (notifObject.isTransient) root.discardNotification(notificationId);
